# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
ESSAYS_1 = [
("校园生活", "The Value of Reading",
 "Reading is a habit that rewards those who keep it. Every evening I spend half an hour with a book, and the quiet moment helps me escape the noise of daily life. Books open a window to different cultures and offer me a chance to think independently. When I meet a difficult passage, I slow down and take notes, which improves my understanding. Over the years, reading has broadened my horizons and enriched my vocabulary. It also teaches me patience, because a good book cannot be finished in a hurry. I would encourage everyone to develop this habit, since the benefits are far greater than the time it costs."),
("校园生活", "Learning to Manage Time",
 "Many students complain that they never have enough time. In my opinion, the problem is not the amount of time but the way we use it. Last term I made a simple plan: I listed every task, decided which one mattered most, and finished it before checking my phone. The result surprised me. I completed my homework earlier and still had energy for basketball. Managing time well does not mean working all day. It means choosing the most important thing and refusing to be disturbed. Once you form this habit, you will feel calmer and more confident, and your grades will improve naturally."),
("友谊", "What Makes a Good Friend",
 "A good friend is not the one who agrees with you all the time. In fact, a true friend dares to point out your mistakes, even though it may cause an awkward moment. I still remember the day my classmate told me that my attitude towards others was rude. I was angry at first, but later I realized she was right. Since then I have learned to listen and to apologize when necessary. Friendship also requires trust and patience. We cannot expect a friend to be perfect, because nobody is. What matters is that you are willing to support each other, especially when one of you is going through a difficult period."),
("家庭", "A Dinner with My Family",
 "In my family, dinner is never just about food. It is the only time when all of us sit down together and share what has happened during the day. My father usually talks about his work, my mother describes the interesting things she has noticed, and I report the progress I have made at school. Sometimes we argue about small matters, but the atmosphere remains warm. I have gradually understood that these ordinary evenings are precious. They remind me that I am loved and supported, no matter how difficult my studies become. When I leave home for university, I will certainly miss this routine."),
("健康", "Exercise Changes More Than Your Body",
 "Some of my classmates think exercise is a waste of time because it takes them away from their books. I disagree completely. Two years ago I was weak and often caught colds. Then I began to run for twenty minutes every morning. At the beginning it was painful, and I wanted to give up. But after a month I noticed that I could concentrate better in class and that I was no longer tired in the afternoon. Exercise does not only strengthen the body; it also reduces stress and improves mood. For students who sit for long hours, regular activity is necessary rather than optional."),
("环境", "Small Actions, Big Difference",
 "Protecting the environment sounds like a huge task that only governments can handle. However, ordinary people can make a real difference. I always carry a bottle instead of buying bottled water, and I refuse plastic bags when shopping. My family separates rubbish and recycles paper and glass. These actions seem tiny, but if millions of people follow them, the effect will be enormous. Besides, saving energy is a matter of attitude. Turning off the light when you leave a room costs nothing, yet it reduces waste. The earth does not need a few perfect heroes; it needs millions of responsible citizens."),
("科技", "Living with Smartphones",
 "Smartphones have changed our lives in ways we could hardly imagine twenty years ago. They allow us to contact friends instantly, pay for goods, and find information within seconds. However, every advantage comes with a price. Many students cannot concentrate because they check their screens every few minutes, and some even feel anxious when the battery is low. In my view, the problem lies not in the device but in our habits. We should set clear limits, for example by keeping the phone away while doing homework. Used wisely, a smartphone is a useful tool; used carelessly, it becomes a master that controls us."),
("科技", "Will Artificial Intelligence Replace Us?",
 "Artificial intelligence is developing faster than most people expected. It can translate languages, write reports and even compose music. Some worry that machines will replace human workers and that many people will lose their jobs. I think this fear is partly reasonable, but it is also exaggerated. Machines are good at dealing with data and repeating tasks, yet they lack imagination and genuine emotion. A teacher, for instance, does more than pass on knowledge; he or she encourages and comforts students. The wise attitude is to accept the change, learn new skills, and cooperate with technology instead of fighting against it."),
("文化", "Why Traditional Culture Matters",
 "In recent years, more young people have become interested in traditional culture. They wear traditional clothes, learn classical instruments and visit museums during holidays. I believe this trend is valuable. Traditions remind us who we are and where we come from. Without them, a society may become rich in material terms but poor in spirit. Of course, we should not simply copy the past. Instead, we ought to understand the meaning behind the customs and combine it with modern life. When a young designer uses traditional patterns in her work, she is not repeating history; she is giving it a new life."),
("阅读", "A Book That Changed My Mind",
 "Last year I read a book about a doctor who worked in a remote village. He had few tools and little money, but he never gave up on his patients. The story impressed me deeply. Before reading it, I had always measured success by salary and reputation. Now I understand that contribution matters more than position. The doctor did not become famous, yet he earned the respect of everyone around him. The book did not offer any easy answers, but it raised questions I had never asked myself. Sometimes a single book is enough to change the direction of a person's thinking."),
("志愿", "A Meaningful Summer",
 "Last summer I joined a volunteer programme and taught children in a mountain village. The conditions were far from comfortable: no air conditioning, limited water, and a long walk to the school. On the first day I was nervous, because I had never stood in front of a class. Gradually I learned to explain things clearly and to encourage shy students. What impressed me most was their curiosity. They asked questions that I could not always answer, which pushed me to prepare more carefully. The experience taught me responsibility and gave me confidence. I returned home tired but grateful."),
("旅行", "Travel Teaches Tolerance",
 "Travel is often described as a way to relax, but I think its greatest value is education. When you visit a strange city, you must deal with unfamiliar food, different customs and unexpected problems. You may get lost, miss a train or misunderstand a local expression. These difficulties force you to become flexible. I once spent a week in a small town where almost nobody spoke English. By the end of the trip I had learned to communicate with gestures and simple words, and I had made several friends. Travel reminds us that our own way of living is not the only reasonable one."),
("成长", "Dealing with Failure",
 "Nobody enjoys failure, but everybody experiences it. When I failed an important examination last year, I felt ashamed and refused to talk about it. For several days I could not concentrate on anything. Later my teacher asked me a simple question: what have you learned from it? That question changed my attitude. I analyzed my weak points, made a new plan and asked classmates for help. This time I did much better. Failure is painful, but it is also honest; it shows exactly where we need to improve. Those who avoid failure usually avoid growth as well."),
("梦想", "Setting a Goal",
 "Many students say they want to succeed, but few of them can describe what success means to them. A vague dream cannot guide daily decisions. Two years ago I decided that I wanted to study medicine, and suddenly my priorities became clear. I paid more attention to biology, read articles about health, and even volunteered in a hospital. The goal did not make my life easier, but it made it meaningful. Of course, plans may change. However, having a direction is better than wandering aimlessly. A clear goal turns ordinary effort into progress."),
("合作", "The Power of Teamwork",
 "Last term our class organized a charity sale. At first everyone had different ideas and the discussion turned into an argument. Then our teacher suggested that we divide the work according to our strengths. Those who were good at drawing designed the posters, careful students managed the money, and outgoing students talked to customers. The event was a great success. I learned that teamwork does not mean that everyone does the same thing. It means that each member contributes what he or she does best, and that differences are treated as resources rather than obstacles."),
("消费", "Shopping Online: Convenience and Caution",
 "Online shopping has become part of everyday life. With a few clicks we can buy almost anything, and the goods often arrive the next day. The convenience is obvious, especially for people who live far from city centres. However, this habit also brings problems. Advertisements are designed to make us buy things we do not need, and low prices sometimes hide poor quality. I have learned to compare several shops before paying and to read comments carefully. Shopping online is neither good nor bad in itself; it depends on whether we stay sensible and control our desires."),
]
